WEBVTT

00:16.684 --> 00:17.977
[alarm beeps]

00:19.854 --> 00:22.064
[theme music playing]

00:58.559 --> 00:59.393
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

00:59.477 --> 01:00.978
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY
WITH SUPERVISION

02:18.722 --> 02:20.307
Tell me, have you always flirted this way?

02:20.391 --> 02:22.852
[gasping]

02:24.436 --> 02:25.437
Are you insane?

02:32.778 --> 02:33.779
[sighs]

02:48.002 --> 02:49.378
No way.

02:54.091 --> 02:55.217
It can't be.

02:57.052 --> 02:58.053
Why?

02:58.137 --> 03:01.223
Why do I feel like Mr. Kang
would just let me get away with anything?

03:02.516 --> 03:03.809
Just one more drink together…

03:10.232 --> 03:12.151
Would you like to…

03:14.111 --> 03:14.945
[stammers]

03:15.029 --> 03:16.822
[Ji-yoon] …have another drink at my place?

03:18.282 --> 03:19.617
No, stop.

03:19.700 --> 03:21.201
Snap out of it, Cha Ji-yoon!

03:21.285 --> 03:25.164
Have me walk you home,
if you still have a long way?

03:27.541 --> 03:29.752
No, I'm only five minutes away.

03:29.835 --> 03:31.420
[sighs]

03:31.503 --> 03:32.338
Thank goodness.

03:34.256 --> 03:35.341
M-My place

03:35.424 --> 03:37.676
is right over there. Just right there.

03:40.596 --> 03:41.513
Have a good night.

03:46.101 --> 03:48.228
[sighing]

03:48.312 --> 03:50.439
Well done, Cha Ji-yoon. Well done.

03:51.732 --> 03:53.233
[sighs] The way I got out of that was…

03:54.485 --> 03:57.529
[groans] That was definitely
the best thing I did this year.

03:57.613 --> 04:01.575
[groans] With my superior?
I almost got involved with my superior.

04:02.534 --> 04:03.869
[sighs] That's just horrifying.

04:04.662 --> 04:06.038
[groans] So horrifying.

04:06.121 --> 04:07.748
Alcohol is my enemy.

04:07.831 --> 04:09.375
[sighs] It gives me strange dreams too.

04:09.458 --> 04:10.584
[groans]

04:11.543 --> 04:12.795
[sighs]

04:15.047 --> 04:16.131
[yelping]

04:35.359 --> 04:36.860
[groans]

04:36.944 --> 04:43.409
Not well done at all! [shrieks, groans]

04:44.159 --> 04:46.912
How am I gonna show my face
at work tomorrow? Damn it.

04:53.627 --> 04:55.129
[sighs]

04:55.212 --> 04:56.672
What are you doing tomorrow?

04:56.755 --> 04:58.007
If you're up for it,

04:58.090 --> 05:00.259
we should meet up again, okay?

05:00.884 --> 05:02.636
Would you like to…

05:04.680 --> 05:08.475
Have me walk you home,
if you still have a long way?

05:09.560 --> 05:10.477
Have a good night.

05:10.561 --> 05:14.773
[pop music plays]

05:16.608 --> 05:17.568
Was that a no?

05:22.489 --> 05:23.949
[sighs]

05:25.200 --> 05:26.744
[sighs] Here it is.

05:30.039 --> 05:31.040
Here. [sighs]

05:38.213 --> 05:39.923
Buy two and get a free one? Of course.

05:40.007 --> 05:41.300
BUTTER COCONUT BISCUIT

05:47.389 --> 05:49.058
-[chuckles] Hello.
-Mmm.

05:50.559 --> 05:51.727
Did you have a rough night?

05:51.810 --> 05:52.853
Yes.

05:55.689 --> 05:57.608
[moans]

05:57.691 --> 05:58.901
Oh, that's better.

05:59.693 --> 06:00.819
[sighs]

06:01.862 --> 06:03.197
That'll be 18.06.

06:03.280 --> 06:04.239
Just a moment.

06:09.078 --> 06:09.953
Hello.

06:10.913 --> 06:12.164
That'll be 1.20.

06:15.042 --> 06:16.085
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon?

06:19.588 --> 06:20.464
[Ji-yoon] Is this

06:21.173 --> 06:22.299
for real?

06:28.430 --> 06:29.473
Uh…

06:30.432 --> 06:33.352
I came out in a hurry, so…

06:39.483 --> 06:41.401
I see you bought a lot of snacks.

06:41.485 --> 06:42.528
Oh, yes.

06:50.410 --> 06:51.578
Would you like a popsicle?

06:56.542 --> 06:57.709
Oh.

06:57.793 --> 07:00.003
If you don't like this,
how about chocolate--

07:18.105 --> 07:19.815
That'll be 20.83.

07:21.233 --> 07:23.735
Huh? He paid for this and didn't take it.

07:25.487 --> 07:27.739
-You know him, right? That guy.
-Sorry?

07:28.824 --> 07:29.658
Me?

07:37.374 --> 07:41.336
[chuckling]

07:42.004 --> 07:44.214
[sighs]

07:55.893 --> 07:57.060
Look, Mom, that lady's

07:57.144 --> 08:00.355
wearing undies
and they look just like Dad's.

08:01.857 --> 08:04.818
No, I'm not. These are silk shorts.
I bought them in Thailand.

08:04.902 --> 08:06.320
-[parent] I'm sorry.
-[chuckles]

08:06.403 --> 08:07.487
[parent] They look nice.

08:09.615 --> 08:12.784
[chuckling]

08:15.495 --> 08:17.247
[Ji-yoon] Hmm? Is he… is he laughing?

08:18.457 --> 08:19.625
Three-No-Man

08:20.334 --> 08:22.044
is actually laughing at me?

08:26.506 --> 08:28.884
[chuckling continues]

08:28.967 --> 08:30.260
I'm going to quit!

08:34.431 --> 08:40.103
EPISODE 2
DREAMING OF QUITTING, STILL CLOCKING IN!

08:42.397 --> 08:44.107
[sighs]

08:45.108 --> 08:47.027
He'd still go to work
even if he was fired.

08:49.947 --> 08:51.782
[sighs]

08:51.865 --> 08:55.369
So, what, you gonna hand him this
and say hi to his face?

08:57.537 --> 08:59.081
[sighs]

08:59.164 --> 09:01.375
[voicemail] The person you are calling
is unavailable.

09:01.458 --> 09:03.168
You'll be redirected to voicemail.

09:04.127 --> 09:05.837
Your boyfriend's been a bit quiet lately.

09:06.505 --> 09:09.007
He used to call at lunchtime
like clockwork.

09:09.091 --> 09:10.217
[chuckles]

09:10.300 --> 09:12.261
He gets like this
when he's too into an experiment

09:12.344 --> 09:15.347
[groans] I hate even thinking about it.
Experiments.

09:18.684 --> 09:20.894
No-ah, I'm going to run to the restroom,
okay?

09:21.645 --> 09:22.521
[No-ah] What?

09:28.110 --> 09:31.488
Oh. Bulgogi combo.
Man, looks like you took all the bulgogi.

09:32.155 --> 09:34.032
Enjoy your meal. Yeah. You too.

09:34.741 --> 09:36.827
Why is it that you
never eat with your own team?

09:36.910 --> 09:39.288
Well, you know,
there's a deep purpose behind that.

09:39.371 --> 09:42.040
He's always hunting for a scoop
even while he's eating.

09:42.124 --> 09:44.501
[chuckles] Old-fashioned intel gathering.

09:45.127 --> 09:47.296
So, are there any new scoops these days?

09:47.379 --> 09:49.256
Anything more shocking than Three-No-Man

09:49.339 --> 09:50.299
becoming our team lead?

09:50.382 --> 09:52.259
[chuckles] You're right.

09:52.342 --> 09:54.177
What's he like to work with?
Are the rumors true?

09:54.261 --> 09:56.346
Not only are the rumors true
about the three No's,

09:56.430 --> 09:59.099
but he’s also a huge workaholic.

09:59.182 --> 10:01.268
-Hasn’t he got a place yet?
-Why?

10:01.351 --> 10:03.645
No one's seen him arrive or even leave.

10:03.729 --> 10:04.688
He's always just here.

10:05.439 --> 10:06.606
Just like he's built-in furniture.

10:08.525 --> 10:10.610
The total opposite of our team lead.

10:10.694 --> 10:12.863
We never see Mr. Ko stay at his desk.

10:13.697 --> 10:14.573
That's right.

10:15.657 --> 10:18.744
-Did you hear about their backstory?
-No.

10:19.411 --> 10:21.330
I heard this through the Secretarial Team.

10:22.164 --> 10:24.041
Mr. Kang was actually with Development,

10:24.124 --> 10:27.210
before briefly moving to Product Planning
to work under Mr. Ko.

10:27.294 --> 10:28.420
-Really?
-Hmm.

10:28.503 --> 10:30.630
Get this, Kang Si-woo was a Sr. Associate,

10:30.714 --> 10:34.051
and he reported his team lead,
Mr. Ko, for taking bribes.

10:34.134 --> 10:35.052
[gasps]

10:35.135 --> 10:36.511
[whispers]
Just so he could take that spot.

10:37.262 --> 10:38.096
What?

10:38.180 --> 10:42.184
Whoa. So that's the reason
Mr. Ko hates Mr. Kang.

10:42.851 --> 10:44.227
He really is the Grim Reaper.

10:44.311 --> 10:46.188
[Kee-tae] He's a total snake that guy.

10:46.271 --> 10:47.606
[No-ah, chuckles] Seriously.

10:47.689 --> 10:51.068
-Hey, keep eating. Keep eating.
-[No-ah clears throat]

10:51.151 --> 10:52.277
[rock music plays]

10:52.361 --> 10:56.782
-[employee 1] Mr. Kang Si-woo?
-[employee 2] I thought he eats alone.

11:05.499 --> 11:06.500
May I join you for lunch?

11:06.583 --> 11:07.584
Please take this seat.

11:09.419 --> 11:10.670
-Right here.
-Stop it.

11:26.937 --> 11:29.064
That is a severely unbalanced meal,
you know.

11:29.689 --> 11:32.192
And I noticed you make your coffee
with two sticks.

11:32.275 --> 11:33.819
That’s damaging to your health.

11:37.072 --> 11:40.367
Oh. [chuckles]

11:40.450 --> 11:42.536
I see you have no rice at all.

11:43.370 --> 11:45.789
Yes, I’d hate to gain belly fat.

11:46.998 --> 11:48.083
[yelping]

11:51.461 --> 11:54.464
[coughing]

12:00.011 --> 12:01.888
You all get coffee after lunch, right?

12:02.764 --> 12:03.723
Well, it's on me today.

12:04.474 --> 12:06.560
-Re-Really?
-Ms. Cha, you should--

12:06.643 --> 12:08.478
I forgot I had something urgent
to take care of,

12:08.562 --> 12:10.564
I apologize.
I will see you all later though.

12:15.610 --> 12:16.945
If you’ll excuse me too.

12:21.032 --> 12:22.701
[Ji-yoon] That scared the hell out of me.

12:23.243 --> 12:24.077
Me too.

12:24.161 --> 12:27.080
He always eats alone.
So why did he decide to sit with us then?

12:27.164 --> 12:28.665
He was acting all buddy-buddy
talking to you.

12:28.748 --> 12:29.833
I know, right?

12:31.626 --> 12:33.753
I'll have an Iced Americano. And you?

12:35.213 --> 12:36.339
I'll have

12:36.423 --> 12:38.133
a chocolate mocha smoothie please.

12:38.758 --> 12:42.512
We'll have one iced Americano
and one chocolate mocha smoothie, please.

12:42.596 --> 12:43.513
Hey.

12:43.597 --> 12:45.140
I'm paying this time though.

12:46.057 --> 12:48.685
-[Si-woo] We'll pay with this card.
-Sure. Please tap it here.

12:48.768 --> 12:49.603
KANG SI-WOO

12:50.228 --> 12:52.564
I thought you had something urgent
to take care of?

12:52.647 --> 12:53.607
I guess you meant coffee.

12:54.900 --> 12:57.527
I was in desperate need
of a caffeine transfusion.

12:57.611 --> 12:59.362
Then, while you get your caffeine fix…

13:00.030 --> 13:01.198
shall we have a chat?

13:01.281 --> 13:04.159
Oh, I left something in the cafeteria.

13:04.242 --> 13:05.869
No-ah, would you grab my coffee?

13:06.578 --> 13:08.830
Wait, but you didn't bring
anything with you.

13:13.960 --> 13:14.836
Thank you.

13:16.671 --> 13:20.675
-What's going on?
-What do you mean?

13:20.759 --> 13:22.719
There's something between
you and Mr. Kang.

13:22.802 --> 13:24.721
[sighs] There's nothing going on.

13:25.305 --> 13:26.431
I guess he's figured it out too.

13:26.515 --> 13:27.474
What?

13:27.557 --> 13:28.892
That you're great at your job.

13:28.975 --> 13:31.102
Isn't he trying to get you
to do some work for him?

13:31.770 --> 13:33.980
We're on different teams.
He can't assign work to me.

13:34.064 --> 13:36.358
Then what? Maybe he just likes you.

13:36.942 --> 13:38.235
That's even more unlikely.

13:38.318 --> 13:42.197
If that's not it, then why is he
following you around like that?

13:52.832 --> 13:54.543
So, did you find the thing you lost?

13:54.626 --> 13:55.460
Yes.

13:56.169 --> 13:58.296
Then, are you free this evening?

13:58.380 --> 13:59.339
Yes.

13:59.422 --> 14:00.423
No!

14:00.507 --> 14:02.634
I have plans that I cannot cancel.

14:02.717 --> 14:03.927
I figured as much.

14:11.476 --> 14:13.979
I told you. He wants to see you
this evening.

14:14.062 --> 14:15.564
You know what this is?

14:15.647 --> 14:17.857
It’s like, when you happen to
see someone’s weakness,

14:17.941 --> 14:20.485
you develop this one-sided sense
of closeness with them, that’s all.

14:20.569 --> 14:21.820
Sorry?

14:21.903 --> 14:24.281
He's just doing it
because he thinks I'm a pushover.

14:25.198 --> 14:26.324
Let's go.

14:37.294 --> 14:38.336
[Hye-ji] Hey!

14:38.420 --> 14:39.546
Lee Hye-ji!

14:40.297 --> 14:41.298
Lee Hye-ji!

14:41.381 --> 14:43.008
[chuckles] It’s been far too long!

14:43.091 --> 14:44.926
Did you miss me a lot or what?

14:45.010 --> 14:46.011
Not at all.

14:46.761 --> 14:49.514
Do you know how long it's been
since I've left the house with a purse

14:49.598 --> 14:51.683
and no diaper bag? It's been far too long.

14:52.475 --> 14:56.313
Hey, all that spicy food I had to avoid
while breastfeeding?

14:56.396 --> 14:57.814
I’m going to eat it all today.

14:57.897 --> 14:58.940
All right.

14:59.024 --> 15:00.317
Let's eat it all!

15:00.400 --> 15:02.861
-[chuckles]
-Let's go. Right this way.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.321
I'm so excited for today.

15:08.408 --> 15:11.161
Do you have any guesses
as to why he wants to see you?

15:11.244 --> 15:12.329
No idea.

15:12.412 --> 15:15.832
Oh. Maybe he wants to make sure
I keep my mouth shut before he leaves.

15:15.915 --> 15:16.916
He's leaving?

15:17.000 --> 15:18.376
Looks like it.

15:18.460 --> 15:20.253
What do you mean, "keep your mouth shut"?

15:20.337 --> 15:21.504
You see,

15:22.422 --> 15:25.842
I kind of accidentally stumbled
onto a really private secret of his.

15:25.925 --> 15:29.638
Meaning he was busted
with a very private secret by you.

15:29.721 --> 15:30.764
Mm-hmm.

15:30.847 --> 15:33.433
And he caught you looking like
a total mess, the kind you

15:33.516 --> 15:34.851
pray no one ever witnesses?

15:34.934 --> 15:36.853
-Hmm.
-And now he’s leaving the company?

15:37.437 --> 15:38.647
Hmm, to put it simply.

15:38.730 --> 15:41.524
The way I see it, this is…

15:42.734 --> 15:43.985
the perfect lead to a confession.

15:44.069 --> 15:45.445
What?

15:45.528 --> 15:47.364
You said he laughed
because of what you were wearing.

15:47.447 --> 15:50.659
You also said, he’s the kind of person…
who never laughs

15:50.742 --> 15:54.245
That means you completely made him
let his guard down.

15:55.080 --> 15:56.915
And now that he’s leaving the company,

15:57.415 --> 16:00.794
there’s no need to worry about getting
caught. He’s gonna ask you out.

16:00.877 --> 16:04.005
I know… but you’re only saying that
because you don’t know him.

16:04.089 --> 16:06.633
That kind of language
doesn’t suit him at all.

16:07.217 --> 16:08.301
You know the type.

16:08.385 --> 16:12.389
He’s the kind of person who always seems
to have a storm cloud over his head.

16:12.472 --> 16:15.767
Better than a guy who’s like… [giggles]
…and who’s all sunshine and flowers.

16:15.850 --> 16:19.020
-[scoffs]
-Just go for it.

16:19.104 --> 16:21.147
Go see if there’s any chemistry there.
Hmm?

16:21.231 --> 16:22.816
If there's no major red flag.

16:23.316 --> 16:25.068
Hey, you get over one man
with another man.

16:25.151 --> 16:26.778
You're wrong about that.

16:26.861 --> 16:29.489
You do it with fried chicken,
beer and going to work.

16:29.572 --> 16:32.534
[sighs] Imagine having all that
and going to work together.

16:32.617 --> 16:33.868
How fun would that be?

16:34.452 --> 16:36.996
Stop with the nonsense and just eat this.
Open up.

16:37.080 --> 16:38.081
NEVER-DIE CHICKEN FEET

16:38.164 --> 16:39.499
[laughing]

16:42.043 --> 16:43.044
[groans]

16:45.422 --> 16:46.297
Gosh, that's spicy.

16:49.759 --> 16:53.138
[electrical humming]

16:58.893 --> 17:02.021
Mr. Kang, looks like
you had a relaxed commute.

17:02.605 --> 17:03.732
Yes.

17:03.815 --> 17:06.067
The urgent work I had to deal with
has settled down for now.

17:06.151 --> 17:08.278
Oh. That's good.

17:09.779 --> 17:12.282
It looks like me coming in early

17:12.365 --> 17:13.992
made things difficult for you.

17:14.075 --> 17:15.952
[scoffs] How could you think that?

17:16.035 --> 17:18.997
How could I think that?
I always come to work on time, and…

17:19.080 --> 17:20.623
-[automated voice] Doors opening.
-Oh, elevator's here.

17:32.093 --> 17:33.803
Please, get in.

17:35.722 --> 17:38.516
[Hye-ji] The way I see it, this is…

17:39.142 --> 17:41.019
the perfect lead to a confession.

17:41.895 --> 17:44.564
Oh, I left something
at the security checkpoint.

17:44.647 --> 17:45.565
Please go ahead.

17:46.733 --> 17:48.568
Can you even leave stuff at security?

17:53.114 --> 17:55.742
[sighs] Seriously?

17:55.825 --> 17:58.286
Why did Hye-ji have to go and say that?

17:58.369 --> 18:00.455
Geez. It's all I think about.

18:01.915 --> 18:03.249
[sighs]

18:04.501 --> 18:05.502
That girl has been

18:06.711 --> 18:07.712
pretty scatterbrained lately.

18:08.671 --> 18:11.257
Weren't you and Ms. Cha
hired at the same time?

18:11.341 --> 18:12.842
Yeah. Oh, my apologies.

18:13.885 --> 18:16.930
Cha Ji-yoon was the first person
in our group promoted to Sr. Associate.

18:17.597 --> 18:20.725
Of course, I do feel
like I'm a bit behind, truly.

18:22.143 --> 18:24.813
I've noticed you have lunch together.
Are you close?

18:25.396 --> 18:27.732
Yes, she's the one
I get along the best with.

18:29.734 --> 18:30.819
That's good.

18:31.402 --> 18:33.279
Wh-What exactly is good?

18:51.798 --> 18:53.174
-Hey.
-Hey.

18:53.258 --> 18:55.093
I told you to wait.
Why are you drinking alone?

18:55.176 --> 18:57.470
Oh… [chuckles]

18:58.388 --> 18:59.264
Give me that.

19:02.141 --> 19:03.393
Hey, hey.

19:04.269 --> 19:05.436
As you already know,

19:06.312 --> 19:10.024
I graduated from a rural college,
so I didn’t have hometown connections.

19:10.108 --> 19:13.444
That's right. How impressive is that, huh?

19:13.528 --> 19:16.698
You don't have any of that
and yet you're doing so well at work.

19:18.867 --> 19:21.119
If I'm doing great,
why haven't I made Sr. Associate?

19:21.953 --> 19:23.121
Hey.

19:23.830 --> 19:25.707
That's because

19:25.790 --> 19:29.127
you've just had terrible luck
with bosses so far.

19:30.128 --> 19:31.129
At this rate,

19:32.130 --> 19:33.423
I'm not sure I can raise

19:34.966 --> 19:36.092
Gyeol and Yul right.

19:36.175 --> 19:38.386
And if you decide to quit then what?

19:38.469 --> 19:40.263
You need to have another job lined up

19:40.346 --> 19:42.181
before you decide
to make a move like that.

19:42.265 --> 19:43.266
Hmm.

19:44.893 --> 19:46.769
That's why I'm trying to find
a new way in.

19:46.853 --> 19:47.687
What?

19:47.770 --> 19:48.813
He's here.

19:51.357 --> 19:53.401
My new lifeline.

19:54.235 --> 19:57.280
[clears throat] Gosh.

19:57.363 --> 19:59.699
What a coincidence
running into you again like this.

19:59.782 --> 20:01.075
-[phone buzzing]
-Oh, gosh. What's this.

20:01.159 --> 20:02.994
Goodness.
You two should go ahead and talk.

20:03.077 --> 20:04.829
I gotta take this call. Yes.

20:04.913 --> 20:06.539
My wife sweet is calling so--

20:06.623 --> 20:07.457
What are you doing right now?

20:07.540 --> 20:09.375
What are colleagues for?
Please help me. Please!

20:12.754 --> 20:14.088
Your timing is impeccable.

20:21.721 --> 20:24.807
[Ji-yoon] He even used my colleague
so he could see me alone?

20:24.891 --> 20:26.726
Trying to get you alone has proven to be,

20:27.518 --> 20:28.728
quite the challenge.

20:28.811 --> 20:29.646
[Ji-yoon] Alone?

20:30.480 --> 20:31.731
Why alone?

20:31.814 --> 20:34.025
Did you have something to say to me?

20:34.108 --> 20:35.401
Yes.

20:36.235 --> 20:37.820
There's something I need to say.

20:37.904 --> 20:38.988
[Ji-yoon] What should I do?

20:42.075 --> 20:43.201
Is here okay?

20:44.577 --> 20:46.329
We can go elsewhere if you'd prefer.

20:46.412 --> 20:48.289
Oh, no. This is fine.

20:48.873 --> 20:49.999
Please, go ahead.

20:51.292 --> 20:52.543
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon, I think

20:53.503 --> 20:54.379
I like you.

20:54.462 --> 20:55.755
I like you.

20:55.838 --> 20:56.965
I like you.

20:57.048 --> 20:58.800
[Ji-yoon] Is he about to confess?

20:58.883 --> 21:02.178
So, Ms. Cha, I’d like you to… go…

21:03.388 --> 21:04.722
[Ji-yoon] Go…

21:06.432 --> 21:09.394
out…

21:10.019 --> 21:12.605
…to go work with me on a task
assigned by the President.

21:13.648 --> 21:14.565
What?

21:14.649 --> 21:18.236
The ice sphere refrigerator
is going back into development.

21:18.319 --> 21:20.321
I'd like you to be on the team.

21:24.659 --> 21:26.285
[spoon clatters]

21:27.370 --> 21:28.329
Oh. No, no, no. Please.

21:28.413 --> 21:30.081
I got it. Let me.

21:33.418 --> 21:35.795
I wish I could disappear right now.

21:40.258 --> 21:41.467
Thank you.

21:47.932 --> 21:51.769
So when you said you had gotten fired…

21:51.853 --> 21:53.521
I got fired from Planning Team 2.

21:53.604 --> 21:54.439
So…

21:54.981 --> 21:56.190
when you suggested

21:56.941 --> 21:58.401
we get a drink last weekend…

21:58.484 --> 22:00.445
I couldn't bring it up
because you were too drunk.

22:00.528 --> 22:01.738
So the reason you kept

22:01.821 --> 22:04.615
following me around these past few days…

22:04.699 --> 22:06.492
You didn't give me
much of a chance to tell you.

22:09.412 --> 22:10.621
[Ji-yoon] It's so mortifying

22:11.414 --> 22:13.041
that it was all in my head, but…

22:16.210 --> 22:17.128
What a relief.

22:17.837 --> 22:19.547
I really appreciate the offer,

22:20.173 --> 22:23.718
but at this time, I have no intention
of switching teams.

22:23.801 --> 22:25.762
May I ask you why that is?

22:25.845 --> 22:28.139
There are some issues
with the voice-activated water dispenser

22:28.222 --> 22:29.640
that I'm working on.

22:30.224 --> 22:32.018
I'd really like to

22:32.101 --> 22:34.437
get everything resolved and see it
launched successfully this year.

22:34.520 --> 22:35.772
If that's your reason,

22:35.855 --> 22:38.483
I'll let you stay in the loop just until
you're all done with the launch.

22:38.566 --> 22:39.901
Oh, no.

22:40.777 --> 22:43.821
Hmm, if I'm being perfectly honest, I'm…

22:45.073 --> 22:46.616
I'm scared of failing right now.

22:48.743 --> 22:50.995
I’d like to work on something
with better chances.

22:54.123 --> 22:55.917
You went to such trouble to bring this up,

22:56.751 --> 22:57.835
I'm really sorry.

22:59.796 --> 23:00.755
I understand.

23:01.964 --> 23:04.967
Do me a favor and keep this between us,
until they announce it.

23:05.051 --> 23:05.885
Sure.

23:07.136 --> 23:08.221
[Kee-tae] Oh, my gosh.

23:08.304 --> 23:10.890
Oh, my goodness. Oh, my goodness.
I'm so sorry. I brought these.

23:10.973 --> 23:13.768
[chuckles] Here. New ones.

23:16.979 --> 23:19.524
-Mr. Kang, can I pour you a drink?
-Sure.

23:21.609 --> 23:23.653
By the way, there’s something
I’ve been wanting to ask you.

23:23.736 --> 23:24.904
All right, I'm listening.

23:24.987 --> 23:26.948
Do you happen to know
about your nickname yet?

23:27.031 --> 23:27.907
Hey.

23:29.283 --> 23:30.118
Are you drunk?

23:30.785 --> 23:31.619
No.

23:31.702 --> 23:33.079
"Three-No-Man," is that right?

23:33.788 --> 23:34.747
So you knew about it.

23:34.831 --> 23:37.208
"No smiles, no people, no apologies."

23:37.291 --> 23:40.128
Whoever came up with that
did a pretty good job if you ask me.

23:42.338 --> 23:43.339
[whispering] So he knew?

23:45.967 --> 23:48.845
Enjoy your drinks
and please use this to pay.

23:48.928 --> 23:50.263
Y-You're already leaving?

23:50.346 --> 23:51.180
Yes.

23:52.140 --> 23:53.432
We had a good talk thanks to you.

23:54.350 --> 23:55.226
See you tomorrow.

23:56.060 --> 23:57.311
[Kee-tae] Wait.

23:57.395 --> 23:59.147
Right. Oh. Uh…

23:59.230 --> 24:00.940
Have a… Have a safe trip home then.

24:02.942 --> 24:03.943
Man.

24:04.610 --> 24:08.114
How dare you use work as an excuse
to get me here?

24:08.197 --> 24:09.991
I mean, what choice did I have.
He said he wanted to see you.

24:10.074 --> 24:12.160
[groans] That really hurt.

24:13.286 --> 24:15.204
Hey, so what did you guys talk about, huh?

24:15.288 --> 24:16.914
It's classified, you punk. [clicks tongue]

24:18.082 --> 24:19.208
"Classified"?

24:19.292 --> 24:21.335
[soft pop music plays]

24:43.316 --> 24:44.942
YEONG-MOOK REPAIR SERVICES

25:02.251 --> 25:03.419
Hi.

25:05.338 --> 25:07.173
-When did you get back?
-A few days ago.

25:07.256 --> 25:08.507
[Yeong-mook chuckles]

25:08.591 --> 25:11.802
I really thought you weren't
coming back ever again.

25:16.224 --> 25:18.768
-What's this?
-I found it on the way here.

25:26.150 --> 25:27.485
Huh, this is…

25:31.822 --> 25:32.823
My goodness.

25:35.243 --> 25:37.870
Well, I’ll need to work
another ten years to earn this.

25:37.954 --> 25:39.538
I'll find you another one
in ten years time.

25:39.622 --> 25:42.124
[chuckles]

25:44.460 --> 25:46.295
Thanks so much.

25:52.260 --> 25:55.513
[peaceful music plays]

25:58.099 --> 26:01.185
[sighs, clicks tongue]

26:02.061 --> 26:03.271
[sighs]

26:03.354 --> 26:06.941
Like I thought. No matter where I go
there’s nothing like your sound system.

26:07.024 --> 26:08.567
There’s nothing special about it.

26:10.611 --> 26:13.364
It's just a bunch of broken parts
that I slapped together.

26:13.447 --> 26:14.448
I like it.

26:14.991 --> 26:16.784
I like that sound in this shop.

26:18.327 --> 26:19.704
I always feel at ease

26:20.871 --> 26:22.039
whenever I come here.

26:22.123 --> 26:23.499
What is going on now?

26:25.126 --> 26:27.670
-Something not going your way?
-How did you know that?

26:27.753 --> 26:29.547
You wouldn't be here for any other reason.

26:29.630 --> 26:31.632
[both chuckle]

26:40.433 --> 26:42.351
There's a mountain of stuff to repair,

26:43.811 --> 26:46.981
get your hands moving
and try to get your thoughts in order.

26:52.445 --> 26:53.821
[sighs]

27:08.502 --> 27:10.629
Wow, this one looks far too difficult.

27:10.713 --> 27:13.215
You need to try the hard ones
if you want to improve.

27:20.306 --> 27:21.807
Your hands have really slowed down.

27:22.433 --> 27:23.309
Hand that over.

27:23.392 --> 27:24.518
Hey, hey. Come on now.

27:25.394 --> 27:26.520
Work on your own thing.

27:26.604 --> 27:28.898
I like things with clear solutions.
[chuckles]

27:30.983 --> 27:33.819
And that is the reason
why you're so bad at dating.

27:33.903 --> 27:35.571
Wow, hitting me where it hurts.

27:36.322 --> 27:37.907
I’m actually on my way back
from getting rejected.

27:37.990 --> 27:39.575
Oh…

27:39.658 --> 27:40.910
Have you taken an interest in someone?

27:40.993 --> 27:43.871
Just give me some advice
on what I should do exactly.

27:43.954 --> 27:45.748
What advice is there to give?

27:46.540 --> 27:49.752
Either drop it and move on,
or keep pushing until it works out.

27:51.587 --> 27:52.421
Is she pretty?

27:52.505 --> 27:54.965
-[scoffs]
-[laughs]

27:55.466 --> 27:56.384
That's good.

27:57.218 --> 27:59.929
Hey, smile like that more often.

28:00.846 --> 28:03.516
[sighs] You live long enough…

28:03.599 --> 28:05.643
you realize how precious smiling days are.

28:37.633 --> 28:40.010
Huh? Hey, a task force notice is up!

28:40.094 --> 28:41.887
[employee 1] Huh?

28:41.971 --> 28:43.389
What kind of task force?

28:43.472 --> 28:45.433
TASK FORCE: A TEMPORARY TEAM
FORMED FOR A SPECIFIC PROJECT

28:45.516 --> 28:47.184
Pretty random timing for a task force.

28:47.268 --> 28:48.644
RECRUITMENT - FUTURE STRATEGY TASK FORCE

28:48.727 --> 28:49.854
Manager Kang Si-woo?

28:50.813 --> 28:53.566
[Ji-yoon] So this is what Mr. Kang
was talking about.

28:53.649 --> 28:56.652
He just became team lead for Team 2,
and he's already leading a task force?

29:01.157 --> 29:02.158
That was it?

29:02.241 --> 29:03.742
Is that why he asked to see you?

29:04.577 --> 29:05.953
-Mm-hmm.
-Are you going to?

29:06.036 --> 29:07.329
I'm not.

29:07.413 --> 29:08.539
[sighs] Thank goodness.

29:09.039 --> 29:10.458
Gosh, I was terrified
at the thought of you

29:10.541 --> 29:12.209
being forced into a hellhole 'cause of me.

29:12.293 --> 29:13.335
What's going on?

29:13.419 --> 29:14.712
Don't just keep it between yourselves.

29:14.795 --> 29:16.505
Spill the beans.
What exactly is happening?

29:21.927 --> 29:24.013
We all assumed that Mr. Kang was done for

29:24.763 --> 29:27.808
after halting operations
of the ice sphere fridge

29:27.892 --> 29:29.226
-did we not?
-That's right.

29:29.310 --> 29:31.020
But, that was not the case.

29:32.188 --> 29:33.522
Just as I thought, Mr. Kang Si-woo,

29:35.149 --> 29:38.277
I don't think your current position
is right for you at all.

29:39.778 --> 29:42.573
You should step down
as the team lead of Product Planning.

29:45.534 --> 29:46.535
As you suggested,

29:47.328 --> 29:49.872
we will completely suspend
the ice sphere refrigerator project.

29:49.955 --> 29:50.956
Instead,

29:51.040 --> 29:55.169
I want you to form a task force and start
developing the fridge from scratch.

29:55.794 --> 29:59.715
Then, I'd like full authority
and responsibility of every step,

29:59.798 --> 30:02.259
from planning all the way to final launch.

30:02.343 --> 30:05.012
Also, I will report directly to you.

30:06.347 --> 30:07.348
Agreed.

30:10.100 --> 30:11.727
Wow, that's crazy.

30:11.810 --> 30:13.354
[employee] Straight to the president?

30:14.271 --> 30:17.233
I mean, just how much faith
does the President have in Mr. Kang

30:17.316 --> 30:18.442
to back him this hard?

30:18.526 --> 30:20.945
It's President Han. You know that.

30:21.028 --> 30:24.156
She's a self-made legend who started
as a regular employee

30:24.240 --> 30:26.033
and made it all the way to President.

30:26.116 --> 30:27.451
She knows better than anyone

30:27.535 --> 30:30.955
what the working-level staff struggle
with, namely, that rigid hierarchy.

30:32.623 --> 30:34.583
And Mr. Kang picked up on that exactly.

30:34.667 --> 30:36.752
[sighs] Okay.

30:36.835 --> 30:39.463
But taking on a project
that's been suspended before…

30:40.047 --> 30:41.340
Is that a step up or step down?

30:41.423 --> 30:46.512
That, right there is exactly the core
of this… change.

30:47.680 --> 30:50.724
Question is,
did she just give Mr. Kang wings to fly,

30:50.808 --> 30:52.184
or did she set a trap for him?

30:52.268 --> 30:53.978
Who would even join him?

30:54.061 --> 30:57.565
Mr. Kang is hard enough to deal with
as is, but what if the project fails too?

30:57.648 --> 31:00.025
Bingo. Yes, No-ah, great point.

31:00.109 --> 31:02.027
So now, what are we supposed to do?

31:02.111 --> 31:03.487
We do absolutely nothing

31:04.363 --> 31:05.489
unless we're told otherwise.

31:06.490 --> 31:10.661
Stay still and play dead.

31:10.744 --> 31:12.538
That is the answer.

31:12.621 --> 31:14.039
Okay?

31:15.708 --> 31:17.334
Mr. Kang is coming this way.

31:17.418 --> 31:19.878
Hello there! [chuckles]

31:23.048 --> 31:23.882
Oh, right.

31:30.389 --> 31:32.474
TECH NECK POSTURE
TECH NECK WARNING!

31:38.272 --> 31:40.816
He snatched my project
from right under my nose.

31:42.067 --> 31:44.820
Not a single person on this team
is allowed to apply.

31:44.903 --> 31:46.989
That would be an act of betrayal
against me.

31:47.072 --> 31:50.200
-Are we clear on that?
-[all] Yes, sir.

31:51.744 --> 31:52.745
[scoffs]

31:53.996 --> 31:55.331
[sighs]

31:56.582 --> 31:58.500
-Ms. Cha.
-Yes?

31:58.584 --> 32:00.002
How's the voice-recognition
dispenser going?

32:00.085 --> 32:02.004
We've been in the testing phase
since switching the mic.

32:02.588 --> 32:05.007
Get over there and check on it
yourself right now.

32:05.090 --> 32:08.093
If that goes wrong on top of everything
else, we are absolutely done for!

32:08.177 --> 32:09.428
Yes, sir.

32:10.888 --> 32:11.722
[Si-woo] Do you

32:12.556 --> 32:15.392
perhaps consider your current duties
to be insignificant?

32:17.353 --> 32:19.938
[Ji-yoon] Mr. Kim, I'm heading down
to check on the test.

32:20.022 --> 32:21.690
[Si-woo] Even the smallest screw

32:21.774 --> 32:24.193
can bring the whole thing down
if it's not fastened right.

32:24.276 --> 32:26.070
Please do your work
with some self-respect.

32:27.029 --> 32:28.197
Are you crying right now?

32:28.280 --> 32:30.032
[sniffles] No, I'm not.

32:35.913 --> 32:37.331
Hold it in.

32:37.414 --> 32:38.832
Crying will do you no good here.

32:59.144 --> 33:00.270
[Ji-yoon] Wow.

33:01.188 --> 33:03.107
Thank goodness I didn't join his team.

33:08.153 --> 33:09.613
TASK FORCE RECRUITMENT STATUS

33:09.697 --> 33:10.948
THERE ARE NO APPLICANTS

33:16.495 --> 33:18.455
-[commentator 1] It's a home run!
-[commentator 2 shouts]

33:18.539 --> 33:21.500
A home run!
What an unbelievable turn of events.

33:21.583 --> 33:22.876
[Ji-yoon] Hey, Buddy,

33:22.960 --> 33:24.628
give me eight ounces of cold water,
will ya?

33:24.712 --> 33:26.922
[commentator 1] The cheers of the fans
are pushing the stadium…

33:27.005 --> 33:28.924
[automated voice]
Dispensing 8 ounces of cold water.

33:29.007 --> 33:30.968
[commentator 2] That was fantastic.

33:31.051 --> 33:32.052
It worked!

33:33.137 --> 33:35.681
It's handling casual speech
and noise just fine.

33:35.764 --> 33:37.015
That's right.

33:37.099 --> 33:39.184
But how did the team even find out

33:39.268 --> 33:41.353
about this budget-friendly microphone
and recommend it?

33:41.937 --> 33:43.689
Well, it's just like you always said,

33:43.772 --> 33:45.566
the Product Planning Team

33:45.649 --> 33:48.652
should always keep some ammo
for moments like these.

33:48.736 --> 33:51.655
Mmm. So you used that extra ammo
to prepare a backup plan in advance?

33:51.739 --> 33:54.283
If I don't have a Plan B ready
ahead of time,

33:54.908 --> 33:56.160
I can't clock out early.

33:56.243 --> 33:58.412
-Exactly. Perfect answer.
-[both chuckle]

33:58.495 --> 34:02.249
Oh, I heard the ice sphere fridge
is getting a task force.

34:02.332 --> 34:03.834
Ah, yes.

34:04.710 --> 34:06.545
Oh, goodness.

34:06.628 --> 34:09.298
I knew when I saw Mr. Kang
at the Gwangju factory,

34:09.381 --> 34:10.966
that he wouldn't just let it slide.

34:12.009 --> 34:16.054
I heard that Mr. Kang actually started out
on the Development Team.

34:16.138 --> 34:17.806
What was he like when he worked there?

34:17.890 --> 34:20.851
He never smiled back then either,
barely said a word.

34:20.934 --> 34:23.270
But everyone respected him.
Say what you want,

34:23.353 --> 34:25.981
but Kang Si-woo has never
lost against a machine.

34:28.317 --> 34:29.318
Hmm.

34:30.736 --> 34:32.821
I'll, uh, let you know
when the final test results are out.

34:33.405 --> 34:34.615
Great, good luck to you.

34:34.698 --> 34:35.783
Thanks.

34:41.955 --> 34:43.999
-Mr. Ko.
-What is it?

34:44.792 --> 34:47.211
I'd like to take the day off tomorrow,
if possible.

34:48.796 --> 34:50.547
It's almost time to clock out

34:50.631 --> 34:52.382
and you want tomorrow off?

34:52.466 --> 34:54.259
Um, what nonsense is this?

34:55.636 --> 34:57.054
I'm sorry, sir.

34:58.096 --> 35:00.891
My sister had to be admitted
to the hospital all of a sudden.

35:00.974 --> 35:03.060
Wait. But why do you need
to take the day off

35:03.143 --> 35:04.853
when it's your sister
who's in the hospital?

35:06.313 --> 35:07.189
Huh?

35:10.150 --> 35:11.443
[scoffs]

35:11.527 --> 35:12.903
Times have changed so

35:13.445 --> 35:16.281
I can’t say a word
about a last-minute request like this.

35:17.616 --> 35:18.575
Do as you wish.

35:19.409 --> 35:20.577
Thank you, sir.

35:23.080 --> 35:24.289
Ms. Cha.

35:25.374 --> 35:26.500
Yes?

35:26.583 --> 35:28.794
Take over Ms. Yoon No-ah’s
overseas market research

35:28.877 --> 35:30.420
and make sure you're done by tomorrow.

35:30.504 --> 35:32.506
Oh, no, I can finish that
as soon as I'm back.

35:32.589 --> 35:33.715
It's urgent though.

35:33.799 --> 35:35.217
[sighs]

35:35.801 --> 35:37.427
Never mind then. I guess I’ll just…

35:37.511 --> 35:38.679
Understood.

35:38.762 --> 35:40.055
I will take care of it.

35:43.475 --> 35:45.894
Just send me the file,
I’ll take care of the rest for you.

35:46.520 --> 35:47.604
I'm sorry, Ms. Cha.

35:47.688 --> 35:50.315
It's all good.
He's doing that on purpose anyway.

35:53.068 --> 35:55.320
All right. Go home, everyone!

35:58.907 --> 35:59.741
OVERSEAS MARKET RESEARCH REPORT

35:59.825 --> 36:01.869
EMAIL: CHA JI-YOON

36:03.412 --> 36:05.581
No-ah, you should go.
Don’t keep your sister waiting.

36:06.290 --> 36:07.291
[sighs]

36:17.801 --> 36:20.429
[sighs] That's how it is.

36:21.763 --> 36:22.848
Love is so selfish

36:24.141 --> 36:25.559
and so foolish. [sighs]

36:26.768 --> 36:28.353
[groans]

36:29.855 --> 36:31.189
I haven't worked late in forever.

36:32.399 --> 36:33.442
[groans]

36:41.033 --> 36:43.619
[electronic voice] Good afternoon,
dear passengers.

36:43.702 --> 36:48.790
This train is a high-speed train
bound for Pohan station.

36:48.874 --> 36:51.752
-Our crew is committed to making sure…
-[sighs]

36:51.835 --> 36:54.046
…you have a comfortable journey.

36:54.129 --> 36:56.298
This train will be departing shortly.

36:56.381 --> 36:57.716
[No-ah] What time do you finish today?

36:57.799 --> 37:00.594
Late because it’s Tuesday, right?
I’m on my…

37:04.181 --> 37:07.643
WHAT TIME DO YOU GET OFF TODAY?
YOU GET OFF LATE ON TUESDAYS, RIGHT?

37:14.149 --> 37:15.484
Everything will be fine.

37:17.110 --> 37:20.948
POHAN UNIVERSITY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY

37:21.031 --> 37:24.076
[student] Come on, Goo-won, we're not
going if you're not coming with us.

37:24.159 --> 37:26.119
-Well in that case, let me think about it.
-Right, guys?

37:31.875 --> 37:33.293
[somber music plays]

37:34.753 --> 37:36.380
Goo-won, is that someone you know?

37:36.463 --> 37:38.548
Yeah. Why don't you head out first?

37:43.595 --> 37:45.097
[sighs]

38:03.824 --> 38:05.784
You can't just come here
without telling me.

38:05.867 --> 38:06.743
Why?

38:07.411 --> 38:08.745
What? Am I not allowed to come here?

38:08.829 --> 38:11.415
No. That's not what I mean.
I told you I've been busy.

38:11.498 --> 38:12.374
Right.

38:12.457 --> 38:14.876
So busy you couldn't come to Seoul
on the weekends

38:14.960 --> 38:15.877
or reply to me?

38:15.961 --> 38:18.588
So I came to you,
is it really worth getting mad about?

38:19.631 --> 38:20.841
[sighs]

38:25.429 --> 38:26.346
I'm sorry.

38:27.723 --> 38:29.725
I mean, I just have a lot
on my plate right now.

38:30.350 --> 38:31.810
I’m a little on edge.

38:32.686 --> 38:35.605
I feel bad that you have to
come to Pohan all the time.

38:36.648 --> 38:37.482
I know you have work.

38:39.109 --> 38:41.445
I took tomorrow off
just for you to yell at me.

38:42.070 --> 38:42.904
Sorry.

38:43.780 --> 38:45.699
-Have you eaten yet?
-No.

38:45.782 --> 38:47.576
I'll treat you to something delicious.

38:47.659 --> 38:49.202
It better be delicious.

38:54.833 --> 38:56.168
[sighs]

39:01.423 --> 39:06.428
[upbeat music playing on phone]

39:51.765 --> 39:53.183
[team lead] But everyone respected him.

39:53.266 --> 39:57.312
Say what you want but Kang Si-woo
has never lost against a machine.

39:58.271 --> 40:00.982
[music continues]

40:30.595 --> 40:32.347
[sighs]

40:33.640 --> 40:36.768
That’s right a sharp… and capable boss.

40:38.353 --> 40:39.437
[sighs]

40:40.605 --> 40:42.315
The type of person I want to work for.

40:48.655 --> 40:50.073
[phone buzzing]

40:53.076 --> 40:54.369
CHO GA-EUL

41:00.876 --> 41:02.836
[tense music plays]

41:02.919 --> 41:03.753
MISSED CALL
CHO GA-EUL

41:08.925 --> 41:09.759
[Ga-eul] Ji-yoon!

41:14.139 --> 41:16.766
[soft music plays]

41:16.850 --> 41:18.226
I missed you.

41:21.855 --> 41:22.856
Why are you here?

41:23.440 --> 41:25.150
This trip was a bit too long, wasn’t it?

41:29.029 --> 41:31.031
I guess you’re pretty angry. Sorry.

41:31.114 --> 41:34.451
Isn't that something you say when you're
a few minutes late to meet someone?

41:35.535 --> 41:38.413
How could you say that
after disappearing for eight months?

41:38.496 --> 41:41.041
Did you really think
you could just say, "I'm back,"

41:41.124 --> 41:43.084
and I'd be like, "Welcome back"?

41:44.502 --> 41:46.421
-Were you waiting long?
-Yes.

41:46.504 --> 41:48.256
At first, I waited out of worry.

41:48.340 --> 41:50.634
Then I waited out of anger.

41:50.717 --> 41:53.094
And later, I waited
just so I can end things properly.

41:54.054 --> 41:57.098
I waited for you while imagining
this moment over and over again,

41:58.016 --> 42:00.060
yet you show up like it was nothing.

42:01.478 --> 42:02.771
Like it was only a couple of days.

42:03.355 --> 42:05.148
How could we break up?

42:05.232 --> 42:07.442
I can't break up with you, Ji-yoon.

42:08.318 --> 42:10.612
Let's go inside.
I have so much to tell you.

42:14.241 --> 42:15.742
I said this over text too,

42:15.825 --> 42:18.787
but I really wanted to tell you
at least once

42:19.663 --> 42:20.914
right to your face.

42:22.332 --> 42:23.625
Cho Ga-eul.

42:24.834 --> 42:26.211
It's been over between us.

42:26.920 --> 42:29.005
Ji-yoon. Ji-yoon!

42:29.089 --> 42:31.132
If you were going to do this,
why'd you come back?

42:31.216 --> 42:32.509
Tell me, what for?

42:35.845 --> 42:37.430
Because I left something important behind.

42:39.724 --> 42:41.268
And it's something I can't live without.

42:43.103 --> 42:45.021
YEAR 2021

42:45.105 --> 42:46.106
Hi there.

42:46.189 --> 42:47.190
Ga-eul.

42:48.358 --> 42:49.901
So, how have you been?

42:50.860 --> 42:53.238
[gentle music plays]

42:56.032 --> 42:57.909
[Ji-yoon]
When did you get back from Australia?

42:59.327 --> 43:00.620
I've been back for ages.

43:01.371 --> 43:04.291
I called you as soon as I got back,
but you changed your number.

43:04.374 --> 43:06.543
I changed it
when I got a new phone from work.

43:06.626 --> 43:08.712
You changed
after you started working there.

43:08.795 --> 43:11.589
We used to stay in touch
all the time before that.

43:15.176 --> 43:16.219
But we’re here,

43:16.803 --> 43:18.221
so I guess it’s all good.

43:20.724 --> 43:22.642
I guess we really are meant to be.

43:23.226 --> 43:25.145
Don't make jokes like that anymore.

43:27.480 --> 43:29.858
You know I had feelings for you
for the longest time.

43:31.484 --> 43:34.154
You don't know how hard it was
to get over you.

43:37.240 --> 43:38.908
Should we make it official then?

43:41.453 --> 43:42.329
What?

43:43.079 --> 43:45.206
Let’s make this official. Ji-yoon.

43:46.833 --> 43:47.792
Do you…

43:52.047 --> 43:53.757
Do you like me?

43:55.884 --> 43:56.968
Mm-hmm.

43:57.594 --> 43:59.179
As more than a friend though?

43:59.262 --> 44:00.096
Mm-hmm.

44:00.638 --> 44:01.848
I really like you.

44:01.931 --> 44:03.099
Since when?

44:04.100 --> 44:07.103
Between your music and your trip
to Australia, I doubt you had the time.

44:09.230 --> 44:10.565
In every spare moment.

44:11.066 --> 44:11.900
What?

44:12.484 --> 44:13.735
In the middle of work…

44:14.819 --> 44:16.363
while I was busy writing songs…

44:17.405 --> 44:18.907
even when I was just spacing out…

44:21.117 --> 44:22.660
You just kept crossing my mind,

44:23.661 --> 44:26.081
like I've left behind something important.

44:27.582 --> 44:28.792
In every spare moment…

44:30.085 --> 44:31.211
for a very long time now,

44:32.629 --> 44:35.298
I've liked you, Ji-yoon.

44:58.238 --> 44:59.906
Take it all. Everything you left behind.

45:00.490 --> 45:02.325
None of this is what I left behind.

45:02.409 --> 45:03.243
You know that.

45:03.827 --> 45:05.662
Then just throw it out for all I care.

45:07.580 --> 45:08.498
I'm sorry

45:09.249 --> 45:10.458
that it took me so long.

45:13.044 --> 45:14.129
If it took you that long…

45:15.296 --> 45:17.173
it means you’d already forgotten about me.

45:18.508 --> 45:19.926
For me, it was…

45:21.094 --> 45:22.345
a painful time,

45:22.429 --> 45:24.055
but also enough time to forget you.

45:26.433 --> 45:28.351
Don't show up
out of the blue like this again.

45:29.102 --> 45:30.895
I'm not happy to see you anymore.

45:32.772 --> 45:33.731
Ji-yoon.

45:35.066 --> 45:38.278
[somber music plays]

46:15.940 --> 46:19.027
[rain pattering]

46:40.632 --> 46:41.716
Hello.

46:45.220 --> 46:47.263
You paid
but didn't take your drink the other day.

46:47.347 --> 46:49.432
Oh, right. Well, it's all good.

46:49.516 --> 46:50.433
Did you not get it?

46:51.100 --> 46:53.895
I gave the drink to that regular of ours,
you were with.

46:56.064 --> 46:58.608
Here's the overseas market report
that Ms. Yoon No-ah was working on.

47:01.110 --> 47:04.030
This here's the profit-and-loss outlook
after replacing the microphone.

47:05.615 --> 47:06.783
[sighs]

47:06.866 --> 47:07.951
About the microphone…

47:08.743 --> 47:10.453
Use the original.

47:11.454 --> 47:12.497
What?

47:12.580 --> 47:14.624
I thought about it all night long,

47:14.707 --> 47:17.585
and replacing the microphone
just feels like a rash decision.

47:18.628 --> 47:21.381
The risk is too high.
Let's just stick to the original.

47:21.464 --> 47:23.841
But we just completed
the first round of testing.

47:24.592 --> 47:26.135
We’re supposed to start
the final round today.

47:26.803 --> 47:28.429
Then hurry over and put a stop to it.

47:29.597 --> 47:30.473
Mr. Ko.

47:31.099 --> 47:32.183
What is this?

47:34.769 --> 47:36.521
Ms. Cha, are you rebelling right now?

47:37.981 --> 47:38.856
That's not it.

47:40.525 --> 47:43.278
But there's the voice recognition issue.

47:43.361 --> 47:45.113
Tell them to stick
to the original microphone

47:45.196 --> 47:47.198
and just fix the software, will you?

47:47.282 --> 47:49.409
But doing that won’t resolve the issue.

47:49.492 --> 47:52.829
And why is that your concern though?
Are you an engineer, Ms. Cha?

47:53.621 --> 47:55.665
Just go and pass on the message.

47:58.084 --> 47:59.502
Mr. Ko, please reconsider--

48:02.380 --> 48:04.007
If you can't do it, then I'll go myself.

48:05.675 --> 48:07.802
Mr. Ko. Mr. Ko!

48:08.469 --> 48:10.513
Please reconsider this, just this once.

48:11.180 --> 48:13.725
The Development Team stayed up for days
running these tests.

48:13.808 --> 48:15.977
Yeah, and that's what those people
are there f--

48:16.686 --> 48:18.104
What the hell? Move!

48:18.187 --> 48:19.522
You haven't changed.

48:19.606 --> 48:20.481
What?

48:20.565 --> 48:23.484
I presume you had
an expensive dinner last night.

48:26.029 --> 48:28.197
[scoffs] What the…

48:29.240 --> 48:30.325
Jesus.

48:30.408 --> 48:32.285
[gentle music plays]

48:47.925 --> 48:49.218
What did you do with my drink, huh?

48:49.302 --> 48:50.553
Huh?

48:52.555 --> 48:55.767
Oh, the one from the convenience store?

48:55.850 --> 48:56.934
Did you drink it?

48:57.018 --> 48:58.353
No. It’s sitting in my fridge…

48:58.436 --> 49:00.730
Then I’ll come by and get it after work.

49:01.314 --> 49:04.025
Oh. I’ll just buy you
the exact same drink.

49:04.108 --> 49:05.193
That won’t do.

49:05.276 --> 49:07.111
Oh, then I'll bring it to you tomorrow.

49:07.195 --> 49:08.821
I have to drink that exact one today.

49:12.492 --> 49:13.326
Okay.

49:31.511 --> 49:34.931
You do know
that was unreasonable, don't you?

49:35.014 --> 49:36.015
[chuckles]

49:37.809 --> 49:39.977
You would've just avoided me
if I'd asked to meet.

49:43.272 --> 49:45.024
What happened after? With Mr. Ko?

49:45.108 --> 49:48.027
The Development Team
went completely ballistic.

49:48.736 --> 49:52.657
Then… everything returned to normal,
like nothing happened.

49:55.284 --> 49:57.370
[Si-woo sighs]

49:59.914 --> 50:01.165
Something similar happened

50:01.916 --> 50:03.376
when I was a Sr. Associate.

50:04.585 --> 50:06.129
Mr. Ko was the team lead,

50:06.713 --> 50:10.216
and he insisted on replacing a capable
part with one from a different supplier.

50:10.299 --> 50:11.467
I looked into it

50:12.760 --> 50:14.804
and found out
that he’d been taking favors.

50:16.806 --> 50:18.891
Get this, Kang Si-woo
was a senior associate

50:18.975 --> 50:22.729
and he reported his team lead,
Mr. Ko, for taking bribes.

50:22.812 --> 50:25.064
-[gasps]
-Just so he could take that spot.

50:25.732 --> 50:27.817
So then what did you end up doing?

50:27.900 --> 50:29.902
I reported it to the Audit Team.

50:30.653 --> 50:32.196
But without conclusive evidence,

50:32.905 --> 50:35.700
they just kept the original supplier
and closed the case.

50:36.492 --> 50:39.704
And then I just got kicked off
of the Product Planning Team.

50:43.666 --> 50:45.710
That must have been really hard.

50:45.793 --> 50:47.003
That's when I made up my mind.

50:48.087 --> 50:50.715
I’d stay out of it all
and just let my work speak for itself.

50:53.176 --> 50:54.218
Join my task force.

50:54.844 --> 50:56.971
I’ll make sure
you never have to deal with that again.

50:57.889 --> 50:59.849
Why are you doing all this for me?

51:00.892 --> 51:02.852
We haven't even
known each other that long.

51:05.188 --> 51:06.272
I've been watching you

51:07.982 --> 51:09.275
for quite some time.

51:09.358 --> 51:12.904
[pop music plays]

51:15.990 --> 51:17.033
Hello, everyone!

51:17.116 --> 51:18.534
My name is Cha Ji-yoon.

51:18.618 --> 51:19.952
[cheers]

51:20.036 --> 51:24.123
One day, I want to create
an automated Snail Bride homemaker system

51:24.207 --> 51:27.460
that takes care of the cleaning,
laundry and dishes

51:27.543 --> 51:28.586
all on its own!

51:28.669 --> 51:30.797
SAEUM NEW HIRE ORIENTATION

51:30.880 --> 51:31.923
What's your ultimate goal?

51:32.006 --> 51:35.176
Obviously, my ultimate goal
is becoming the president of SAEUM.

51:35.259 --> 51:37.804
[all cheering]

51:39.138 --> 51:42.099
[Si-woo] I found one new hire’s
ambitious goal to be quite impressive.

51:42.975 --> 51:44.936
Still, I assumed it wouldn’t last long,

51:45.019 --> 51:46.938
just like with any other rookie.

51:47.021 --> 51:50.024
[Ji-yoon] What if there were
a talking companion robot vacuum?

51:50.107 --> 51:53.486
If you combine a robot vacuum cleaner
with a voice assistant service,

51:53.569 --> 51:55.863
it can evolve into a talking robot vacuum.

51:55.947 --> 51:58.407
Users could give it
a name of their choice,

51:58.491 --> 52:00.952
and whenever they have a question
or just need someone to talk to,

52:01.035 --> 52:03.246
they could chat with their vacuum.

52:03.913 --> 52:06.749
"Ms. Bokja,
will it stop raining tomorrow?"

52:08.000 --> 52:10.837
Uh, maybe Ms. Bokja is a little tacky.

52:10.920 --> 52:12.880
[Si-woo] But that rookie was different.

52:12.964 --> 52:15.758
She knew exactly what she wanted
right from the very beginning.

52:17.385 --> 52:18.219
Enough already.

52:18.302 --> 52:19.303
I know it's a machine,

52:19.387 --> 52:21.514
but it has to feel
like it has real emotions.

52:26.185 --> 52:27.103
Huh?

52:30.940 --> 52:33.693
[Si-woo] Even as she gained seniority,
she refused to compromise,

52:33.776 --> 52:35.736
and I found myself rooting for her.

52:37.321 --> 52:39.866
But when I saw you again at the factory,

52:39.949 --> 52:41.158
you'd changed a lot.

52:41.242 --> 52:43.953
And then we can gradually work on
perfecting the ice quality from there?

52:44.036 --> 52:46.956
To be honest, I was disappointed.

52:47.582 --> 52:51.127
But then I saw your notebook and realized.

52:51.794 --> 52:52.920
You hadn't changed.

52:54.213 --> 52:55.590
You were just hiding.

52:55.673 --> 52:58.342
And then I thought to myself,
"I don't want to let this person go."

53:00.011 --> 53:02.430
The way I see it… you deserve

53:02.513 --> 53:05.683
to aim a lot higher
than what you have so far.

53:05.766 --> 53:07.810
It would be a real shame to keep all that

53:08.436 --> 53:11.063
potential locked away in a notebook.

53:11.147 --> 53:13.733
[gentle music plays]

53:13.816 --> 53:15.067
I'll give you time to think.

53:18.112 --> 53:19.280
As for my drink,

53:20.072 --> 53:21.407
thank you for holding on to it.

53:33.961 --> 53:34.795
What?

53:37.965 --> 53:39.425
Those words, make me…

53:41.719 --> 53:44.680
feel… I feel… giddy.

54:07.078 --> 54:09.497
[scoffs] She must've run here.

54:22.802 --> 54:25.638
[No-ah] Babe, should I move down here
once we’re married?

54:26.722 --> 54:27.974
[Goo-won] What about your job?

54:28.557 --> 54:30.184
Well, I could find a job here

54:30.267 --> 54:31.686
and maybe go into the public-sector.

54:32.645 --> 54:35.189
Come on, why would you leave
a big company everyone's

54:35.272 --> 54:36.649
dying to get into?

54:37.650 --> 54:40.653
Even after you get your degree,
you won’t be able to come to Seoul.

54:40.736 --> 54:43.864
What's the point of getting married
if we still can't see each other often?

54:47.368 --> 54:48.828
[clears throat]

54:48.911 --> 54:50.413
You’re gonna be late to class
because of me.

54:50.496 --> 54:51.956
You should get going.

54:52.748 --> 54:53.916
Mm-hmm.

54:54.500 --> 54:55.459
Bye then.

55:01.716 --> 55:02.675
No-ah!

55:06.429 --> 55:07.430
No-ah, let's just…

55:07.513 --> 55:12.685
[electronic voice] Attention, passengers.
The 559 train bound for Seoul

55:12.768 --> 55:13.894
is now arriving at Platform 7.

55:13.978 --> 55:15.312
-[train horn blares]
-…break up.

55:15.396 --> 55:17.898
[electronic voice]
Please stand behind the yellow line.

55:17.982 --> 55:22.653
Passengers, please check your boarding
position before stepping onto the train.

55:22.737 --> 55:24.155
Enjoy your trip.

55:25.948 --> 55:30.411
[sad music plays]

55:47.303 --> 55:48.721
[breathing shakily]

55:49.472 --> 55:50.514
[gasps] No-ah!

55:51.348 --> 55:52.224
What's wrong?

55:52.308 --> 55:53.684
Oh, my gosh.

55:53.768 --> 55:54.685
Are you sick?

55:55.269 --> 55:56.437
Ms. Cha…

55:56.520 --> 55:57.855
Let's get you to the hospital. Get up.

55:58.773 --> 56:01.484
I can't. I already took yesterday off.

56:01.567 --> 56:03.986
You can't work in this state, okay.

56:05.738 --> 56:08.783
What? Taking the day off yesterday

56:08.866 --> 56:10.076
and you’re leaving early today?

56:11.368 --> 56:13.496
I make sure to only get sick after work

56:13.579 --> 56:15.039
and on weekends.

56:15.122 --> 56:17.458
Taking care of yourself
is part of the job!

56:19.126 --> 56:20.044
Ms. Yoon No-ah.

56:22.546 --> 56:23.380
Mr. Ko.

56:23.464 --> 56:26.300
Ms. Yoon No-ah, what exactly
are your strengths?

56:26.383 --> 56:27.551
Huh?

56:27.635 --> 56:29.261
You’re not a fast worker like Ms. Cha.

56:29.345 --> 56:30.721
And you don't have any guts either!

56:30.805 --> 56:33.140
Ms. No-ah is very unwell at the moment.

56:33.224 --> 56:35.684
Let her go home for now
and you can speak to her again tomorrow.

56:35.768 --> 56:38.771
Seeing as you’re in the same outfit
as the other day,

56:39.480 --> 56:41.190
it seems you lied
about your sister being sick

56:41.273 --> 56:43.067
and went on vacation with your boyfriend.

56:43.150 --> 56:46.195
-Mr. Ko!
-Why don't you get married already?

56:46.278 --> 56:48.614
Stop wasting everyone’s time,
showing up to just collect a paycheck!

56:48.697 --> 56:50.616
Please just stop this!

56:55.746 --> 56:57.081
Diminishing or mocking

56:57.164 --> 56:59.625
an employee’s performance or abilities
without a proper reason.

57:00.584 --> 57:03.629
Pressuring them not to use their vacation,
or their sick leave

57:04.547 --> 57:06.924
and spreading gossip or rumors
about their personal life.

57:07.842 --> 57:10.928
Every single word you just said
to Ms. Yoon No-ah,

57:11.554 --> 57:13.389
constitutes workplace harassment.

57:13.973 --> 57:15.015
[Young-sam scoffs]

57:15.641 --> 57:17.518
Are you saying you’ll report me
or something?

57:17.601 --> 57:19.270
I really don’t want to do that.

57:20.855 --> 57:22.356
So I ask you to please…

57:23.816 --> 57:26.318
stop speaking to us so disrespectfully
from now on.

57:29.947 --> 57:31.031
I ask you kindly.

57:39.832 --> 57:41.500
I didn’t expect this from you,

57:42.418 --> 57:43.294
Ms. Cha.

57:44.336 --> 57:45.671
[exhales sharply]

57:47.381 --> 57:48.340
Fine.

57:49.133 --> 57:50.426
Let's do that.

57:50.509 --> 57:51.510
Going forward,

57:51.594 --> 57:54.805
I will be very polite to
each and every one of you.

57:55.389 --> 57:56.390
Oh.

57:57.183 --> 58:00.352
Ms. Yoon No-ah, since you're feeling sick,
you may leave early.

58:01.896 --> 58:02.980
And Ms. Cha Ji-yoon.

58:04.732 --> 58:06.400
Please analyze our competitors’ trends

58:06.483 --> 58:09.153
over the last three years
and prepare a report for me.

58:10.112 --> 58:12.072
This is not an unfair assignment,

58:12.156 --> 58:16.577
but a perfectly legitimate request
that is completely necessary for the team.

58:25.085 --> 58:26.545
What are you staring at exactly?

58:42.311 --> 58:44.146
Why would you pick a fight with him?

58:44.230 --> 58:45.189
Ms. Cha.

58:46.440 --> 58:47.316
[Ji-yoon] Let's go.

58:50.027 --> 58:51.570
-[whimpers]
-Go straight to the hospital.

58:51.654 --> 58:53.864
I can't come with you,
so call your sister.

58:54.573 --> 58:56.617
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

58:56.700 --> 58:59.411
It's not your fault. Get going now.

59:09.421 --> 59:12.174
[breathes shakily]

59:23.644 --> 59:25.646
[lighthearted music plays]

59:39.034 --> 59:40.536
PRODUCT PLANNING TEAM 1
CHA JI-YOON

59:41.704 --> 59:42.705
[sighs]

59:47.584 --> 59:49.295
Hi, Mom! [chuckles]

59:49.378 --> 59:51.463
I'm officially starting work tomorrow!

59:51.547 --> 59:53.590
I've been assigned
to the Product Planning Team.

59:53.674 --> 59:56.719
My name and face are right here
on my employee ID! [chuckles]

59:56.802 --> 59:59.013
[Mom] I'm actually at the shop right now
to buy rice cakes

59:59.096 --> 01:00:00.556
for the whole neighborhood.

01:00:01.223 --> 01:00:03.017
What? Why would you buy that?

01:00:03.100 --> 01:00:06.395
[Mom] My daughter got a job at a major
corporation, so it’s the least I can do.

01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:08.272
So what is this product team?

01:00:08.355 --> 01:00:09.898
What will you be doing there?

01:00:09.982 --> 01:00:11.984
You wouldn't know even if I told you.

01:00:12.067 --> 01:00:15.821
I'm going to work so hard, you know?

01:00:15.904 --> 01:00:18.991
Actually, I’m just going to work
in this place forever and ever.

01:00:19.074 --> 01:00:21.410
[chuckles] I’m heading home now.

01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:22.578
Let’s have a party tonight.

01:00:56.862 --> 01:00:59.365
COMPETITOR TRENDS REPORT, 2023-2025

01:01:06.080 --> 01:01:08.582
[Ji-yoon] Product Planning Team 1.
Cha Ji-yoon.

01:01:08.665 --> 01:01:11.168
Rank: Senior Associate.

01:01:11.251 --> 01:01:13.253
I hereby submit my resignation
for personal reasons…

01:01:13.337 --> 01:01:14.171
RESIGNATION URGE STICKERS

01:01:14.755 --> 01:01:17.466
…so I ask that it be processed…

01:01:21.470 --> 01:01:22.930
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

01:01:23.013 --> 01:01:24.598
"Personal reasons," my ass.

01:01:25.516 --> 01:01:26.975
You all probably look at me,

01:01:27.059 --> 01:01:30.479
and see nothing
but a lowly corporate slave.

01:01:30.562 --> 01:01:32.356
But I want you to know

01:01:32.439 --> 01:01:36.360
that I was once a bright-eyed,
passionate employee

01:01:37.111 --> 01:01:43.617
who walked through those doors
full of hopes and wonderful dreams.

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:46.662
Does it make you feel good
to insult my character?

01:01:46.745 --> 01:01:49.748
To look down on me
and treat me like trash?

01:01:49.832 --> 01:01:52.084
This place is toxic and pathetic.

01:01:52.167 --> 01:01:56.046
[scoffs] I am walking out of here
on my own terms, everyone.

01:01:56.130 --> 01:02:00.134
Have a nice life. As for me,
I'm off to find my happiness.

01:02:00.217 --> 01:02:02.136
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
CONFIRM SUBMISSION

01:02:06.890 --> 01:02:08.559
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?
CANCEL - CONFIRM

01:02:13.605 --> 01:02:14.940
[sighs] Damn it.

01:02:17.568 --> 01:02:18.777
[sighs]

01:02:27.995 --> 01:02:31.373
How sad and pathetic can you really be?
Huh?

01:02:31.457 --> 01:02:33.500
[sighs] I couldn’t even throw these away.

01:02:49.224 --> 01:02:50.434
[sighs]

01:03:16.460 --> 01:03:19.922
HOT AIR UV SYSTEM
SHOE CARE DEVICE

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:21.507
[Si-woo] I’m here from the future.

01:03:21.590 --> 01:03:22.716
This has already been released.

01:03:40.317 --> 01:03:42.194
[Ji-yoon]
Washer and dryer combined into one?

01:03:42.778 --> 01:03:44.655
[Si-woo]
Now it's possible with a single machine.

01:03:45.572 --> 01:03:46.698
[Ji-yoon] How should I open this?

01:03:47.824 --> 01:03:50.035
[Si-woo]
Touch lightly to automatically open doors.

01:03:51.245 --> 01:03:54.039
Why did he have to go scribble
all over someone else's notebook?

01:03:54.122 --> 01:03:55.999
[gentle music plays]

01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:58.794
Did he think using a pencil was okay?

01:04:02.548 --> 01:04:05.676
Can't we turn everything into away mode,
like with a hotel key card?

01:04:06.426 --> 01:04:07.553
[Si-woo] It's possible.

01:04:07.636 --> 01:04:11.431
You just design a single software
to control multiple hardware devices,

01:04:11.515 --> 01:04:15.352
like using a single smartphone
to control all your home appliances.

01:04:20.857 --> 01:04:22.317
[Ji-yoon] Ice spikes?

01:04:29.700 --> 01:04:30.534
[Si-woo] Good!

01:04:31.118 --> 01:04:32.369
[cries]

01:04:33.453 --> 01:04:34.621
Mr. Kang…

01:04:36.331 --> 01:04:37.791
He’s seriously the worst.

01:04:49.636 --> 01:04:51.138
[inspirational music plays]

01:05:03.483 --> 01:05:05.527
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?

01:05:20.459 --> 01:05:22.669
SUBMIT THIS DOCUMENT?
CANCEL - CONFIRM

01:05:30.344 --> 01:05:32.220
[Ji-yoon]
There's no such thing as the perfect boss.

01:05:34.765 --> 01:05:36.767
Just like there isn't a perfect lover.

01:05:39.770 --> 01:05:41.313
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

01:05:41.396 --> 01:05:43.023
[upbeat music plays]

01:05:43.106 --> 01:05:47.778
Just wear a pair of acupressure slippers,
and it'll solve everything.

01:05:49.154 --> 01:05:50.614
Oh.

01:05:50.697 --> 01:05:51.907
Good morning, Mr. Ko. Everything good?

01:05:51.990 --> 01:05:53.909
Mm-hmm. Good morning, Ms. Cha.

01:06:00.165 --> 01:06:01.166
What the…

01:06:01.249 --> 01:06:03.794
[Ji-yoon] At the end of the day,
this is just a game of this or that.

01:06:03.877 --> 01:06:06.046
[Young-sam] Why are you going that way?
Wrong way. Huh?

01:06:06.129 --> 01:06:07.172
Huh?

01:06:07.255 --> 01:06:10.175
[Ji-yoon] Even if tomorrow's me
regrets the choices I make today…

01:06:10.759 --> 01:06:11.927
[employee] What?

01:06:12.010 --> 01:06:15.472
Sr. Associate Cha Ji-yoon, checking in.
I’d like to apply for the task force.

01:06:17.974 --> 01:06:18.975
[Young-sam] Hey!

01:06:22.437 --> 01:06:24.231
[Ji-yoon] All I can do is choose
the lesser

01:06:24.314 --> 01:06:26.483
evil, instead of the absolute worst.

01:06:30.404 --> 01:06:31.405
I look forward to this.

01:06:35.409 --> 01:06:36.660
I look forward to it too.

01:06:36.743 --> 01:06:39.079
[theme music playing]

01:07:29.880 --> 01:07:33.633
With the time we have left, we have
to be able to make the perfect ice sphere.

01:07:33.717 --> 01:07:35.886
-Would that be possible?
-Fail. Fail.

01:07:35.969 --> 01:07:37.512
-[groans]
-[sighs]

01:07:37.596 --> 01:07:38.930
I'm wiped.

01:07:41.308 --> 01:07:42.976
[Si-woo] Please change your keyboard
to a silent keyboard.

01:07:43.059 --> 01:07:45.812
[Ji-yoon] I'll clock out on time
no matter what and order fried chicken.

01:07:45.896 --> 01:07:47.606
This is awkward as hell.

01:07:48.648 --> 01:07:51.401
[Ga-eul] I’m finally done
composing our song.

01:07:52.527 --> 01:07:54.738
Would you mind leaving us?

01:07:55.363 --> 01:07:56.740
I have something to tell her.

01:07:56.823 --> 01:07:59.117
So I assume you’ll be free this weekend.

01:07:59.201 --> 01:08:00.827
[Ji-yoon] Lovesick, really?
